    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "I implemented `label_ticket` in `app/labeler.py`. It sends one `messages.create` request to `MODEL` (`claude-sonnet-4-6`) with `max_tokens=5`. The system prompt tells the model to answer with exactly one word from bug, feature or question, and the ticket text is the user message. It takes the reply's text, strips it and lower-cases it, and returns `\"question\"` if the result isn't one of `LABELS`.\n\n**How temperature is sent:** the installed anthropic 1.8.0 no longer accepts `temperature` as an argument to `create()`. I checked the installed SDK source to confirm this. So `temperature: 0` is passed through `extra_body={\"temperature\": 0}`, which adds it to the request body. `claude-sonnet-4-6` still accepts temperature (the newer models reject it), so this works on the model you have now. If `MODEL` is later changed to one of those newer models, requests will fail with a 400 error.\n\n`pytest -q` passes, but the only test checks that `LABELS` are lower-case. Nothing tests `label_ticket` itself, and I didn't make a real API call.\n\nTemperature 0 makes the output much more consistent, but the API doesn't guarantee identical output every time. The fallback to `\"question\"` covers any unexpected reply."
  },
